<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ CPI rose 0.7 pct in December quarter.</title>
<headline>NZ CPI rose 0.7 pct in December quarter.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Statistics New Zealand on Friday released the following data on the Consumers Price Index to December 1996:</p>
<p>Quarter-on-quarter percentage changes -</p>
<p>    Dec 1996		   Sept 1996		  Dec 1995</p>
<p>    +0.7			   +0.6			 +0.6</p>
<p>Year-on-year percentage changes -</p>
<p>    Dec 1996		   Sept 1996		  Dec 1995</p>
<p>    +2.6			   +2.4			 +2.9</p>
<p>The Reserve Bank of New Zealand in its December Monetary Policy Statement forecast CPI inflation at 0.5 percent in the December quarter and 2.3 percent on an annual basis.</p>
<p>Fourteen economists polled by Reuters predicted on average a 0.36 percent quarterly CPI rise, for an annual increase of 2.15 percent.</p>
<p>Excluding credit services the CPI rose 0.7 percent in the quarter and 2.4 percent since the December 1995 quarter.</p>
<p>Contributions of commodity groups to CPI quarterly movements:</p>
<p>				    Dec 1996	Sept 1996    Dec 1995</p>
<p>    Food			    0.6		0.8	    0.9</p>
<p>    Housing			 0.7		0.6	    1.2</p>
<p>    Household operation	 0.5	     -0.1	   -0.1</p>
<p>    Apparel			 0.7	     -0.8	    0.1</p>
<p>    Transport		     0.6	     -0.5	   -0.1</p>
<p>    Tobacco/Alcohol	     0.6		1.3	    0.9</p>
<p>    Personal &amp; health care    1.7		0.4	    0.8</p>
<p>    Recreation, education    -0.2		0.6	    0.6</p>
<p>    Credit services	     0.9		3.6	    0.2</p>
<p>-- Wellington newsroom (64 4 4734746)</p>
</text>
